{"name":"Tiger Tail","hex":"#fee9c4","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tiger tail","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An orange-flavoured ice cream with black licorice swirl."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tiger_tail"}],"entries":[{"title":"Thlocklo Tustenuggee","blocks":[{"text":"Thlocklo Tustenuggee was one of the most prominent Seminole leaders in the Second Seminole War. He spoke English fluently, and also spoke Muscogee. Tustenuggee was one of the three leaders of the 300 Seminoles who fought in the battle that became known as the Dade Massacre. During the war, he and Halleck Tustenuggee, another prominent Seminole leader in the war, met with General Walker Keith Armistead to negotiate, but negotiations broke down and the war resumed. As the war waned, Armistead used money to bribe several Seminole leaders to surrender, but Tustenuggee refused to be bribed and he continued to lead his band in fighting. When the war ended, his Seminole band was one of the few that remained in Florida."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Thlocklo_Tustenuggee_Tiger_tail.jpg/330px-Thlocklo_Tustenuggee_Tiger_tail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thlocklo_Tustenuggee"},{"title":"Baby Doll","blocks":[{"text":"Baby Doll is a 1956 American black comedy film directed by Elia Kazan and starring Carroll Baker, Karl Malden and Eli Wallach. It was produced by Kazan and Tennessee Williams, and adapted by Williams from two of his own one-act plays: 27 Wagons Full of Cotton and The Unsatisfactory Supper. The plot focuses on a feud between two rival cotton gin owners in rural Mississippi."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/69/BabyDollPoster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baby_Doll"},{"title":"Tiger","blocks":[{"text":"The tiger is a large cat and a member of the genus Panthera native to Asia. It has a powerful, muscular body with a large head and paws, a long tail and orange fur that fades to white in parts, with black, mostly vertical stripes. It is traditionally classified into nine subspecies, though some recognise only two subspecies, the mainland Asian tiger and the Sunda Islands tiger."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Bengal_tiger_%28Panthera_tigris_tigris%29_female_3_crop.jpg/330px-Bengal_tiger_%28Panthera_tigris_tigris%29_female_3_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tiger"},{"title":"Tail","blocks":[{"text":"The tail is the elongated section at the rear end of a bilaterian animal's body; in general, the term refers to a distinct, flexible appendage extending backwards from the midline of the torso. In vertebrate animals that evolved to lose their tails, the coccyx is the homologous vestigial of the tail. While tails are primarily considered a feature of vertebrates, some invertebrates such as scorpions and springtails, as well as snails and slugs, have tail-like appendages that are also referred to as tails."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/White-tailed_deer%2C_tail_up.jpg/330px-White-tailed_deer%2C_tail_up.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tail"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/41/Carroll_Baker_in_Baby_Doll_trailer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/41/Carroll_Baker_in_Baby_Doll_trailer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Carroll Baker plays Baby Doll Meighan","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACarroll_Baker_in_Baby_Doll_trailer.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/58/Eli_Wallach_in_Baby_Doll_trailer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/58/Eli_Wallach_in_Baby_Doll_trailer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Eli Wallach plays Silva Vacarro","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEli_Wallach_in_Baby_Doll_trailer.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/21/Karl_Malden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/21/Karl_Malden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Karl Malden plays Archie Lee Meighan","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKarl_Malden.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Mildred_Dunnock%2C_1956.jpg/330px-Mildred_Dunnock%2C_1956.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Mildred_Dunnock%2C_1956.jpg/330px-Mildred_Dunnock%2C_1956.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mildred Dunnock plays Aunt Rose Comfort","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMildred_Dunnock%2C_1956.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Jack_Garfein%2C_Carroll_Baker%2C_and_Elia_Kazan.png/500px-Jack_Garfein%2C_Carroll_Baker%2C_and_Elia_Kazan.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Jack_Garfein%2C_Carroll_Baker%2C_and_Elia_Kazan.png/500px-Jack_Garfein%2C_Carroll_Baker%2C_and_Elia_Kazan.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Jack Garfein, Carroll Baker, and Elia Kazan on the set of Baby Doll","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJack_Garfein%2C_Carroll_Baker%2C_and_Elia_Kazan.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Cardinal_Francis_Spellman_1946.jpg/500px-Cardinal_Francis_Spellman_1946.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Cardinal_Francis_Spellman_1946.jpg/500px-Cardinal_Francis_Spellman_1946.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cardinal Francis Spellman, Archbishop of New York, protested the film.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACardinal_Francis_Spellman_1946.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Baby_Doll_ad_-_11_December_1956.jpg/500px-Baby_Doll_ad_-_11_December_1956.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Baby_Doll_ad_-_11_December_1956.jpg/1280px-Baby_Doll_ad_-_11_December_1956.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Baby_Doll_ad_-_11_December_1956.jpg/500px-Baby_Doll_ad_-_11_December_1956.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Theatrical advertisement from 1956","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABaby_Doll_ad_-_11_December_1956.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Tiger_distribution.png/500px-Tiger_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Tiger_distribution.png/1280px-Tiger_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Tiger_distribution.png/500px-Tiger_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_c